  "mother": {
    "preparation": {
      "model_calls": 1,
      "phase": "preparation",
      "plan": {
        "A": "Own the algorithmic bottleneck investigation. Produce oracle-valid serial candidates replacing per-column quadratic bubble sorting and quadratic mode counting with an efficient sort plus a linear run scan; consider a small-size/mostly-sorted fallback only if measurements justify it. Preserve median behavior, the reference's sorted tie choice for mode and -1-for-no-duplicate behavior, and the post-sort accumulation order used for variance. Test odd/even row counts, duplicate ties, negatives, zeros, and varied matrix shapes; do not specialize to benchmark values.",
        "B": "Own independent single-threaded dataflow work. Investigate safe reductions, allocation/layout/cache improvements, and input/output overhead while retaining the column-major representation and exact seven-line formatting. Fuse work only when it does not change floating-point accumulation order; assess replacing pow(x,2) only after correctness validation. Avoid fast-math, reordered/Welford reductions, or mode shortcuts that can alter observable results. The 10 ms baseline means startup and parsing overhead may matter as much as arithmetic.",
        "C": "Own a bounded multicore candidate for the ARM64 four-core target. Keep parsing/output deterministic and parallelize independent per-column work, preserving each column's reference arithmetic and sorting semantics. Evaluate scheduling, false-sharing avoidance, and a workload-based serial fallback so thread startup does not hurt small inputs or few-column matrices. Do not oversubscribe, rely on changed target/compiler settings, or parallelize reductions in a way that changes their numerical result.",
        "G": "Integrate only measured, independently correct artifacts from A/B/C. Revalidate every candidate and each combination against the oracle, retain the exact output format, and benchmark combinations separately: sorting, serial dataflow, and threading gains are not assumed additive. Given the valid baseline mean of 0.0100496 s with noticeable sample variation, select the simplest candidate with a credible improvement and retain a serial path where parallel overhead loses. Do not modify tests, oracle, budgets, target, permissions, or specialize to known inputs.",
        "analysis": "The valid baseline is already about 10.05 ms on a four-core ARM64 machine, so small gains may be noise. The clearest source-level asymptotic cost is O(columns·rows²) bubble sorting; mode is also quadratic after sorting. Columns are contiguous in memory, making per-column serial or parallel work natural. Arithmetic and harmonic means are computed before sorting, whereas variance is accumulated after sorting; changing that order can change printed floating-point results. Correctness also includes seven lines, one-decimal values, trailing spaces, and source-compatible mode/tie behavior. Research should therefore prioritize an efficient semantics-preserving sort/run-mode pipeline, then independently test low-level serial and carefully thresholded parallel variants on broad valid inputs."
      },
